; A deliberately chunky silhouette: the hero's bulk is competence, and the
; charge telegraph has to be readable at distance, so the snout gives the body
; an unmistakable facing.
;
; `floor_snap_length` is 0.8, well above Godot's 0.1 default. A charge tops out
; at 20 m/s and the greybox has a slope: at that speed the surface falls away
; faster than a straight-line step can follow, so the body leaves the floor,
; is_on_floor() goes false, and everything keyed off standing on the ground
; stops happening. See CLAUDE.md — it cost the old ramp half its speed.
[node name="HeavyPlayer" type="CharacterBody3D" groups=["player"]]
collision_layer = 2
collision_mask = 69
floor_max_angle = 0.872665
floor_snap_length = 0.8
script = ExtResource("1")
jump_fx = ExtResource("puff")
impact_fx = ExtResource("ring")
sfx_jump = ExtResource("sjump")
sfx_land = ExtResource("sland")
sfx_charge = ExtResource("scharge")

